  "slug": "artist:guy",
  "name": "Guy",
  "editorial_article": "Guy formed in the late 1980s as a foundational group for the new jack swing movement, led by the producer and songwriter Teddy Riley. Their self-titled 1988 debut album established the group at the center of the emerging fusion of hip hop rhythms and urban contemporary R&B. The group achieved significant commercial success with hits including 'Groove Me', which reached number four on the US R&B charts, and 'Teddy's Jam', which climbed to number five on the same chart. Throughout their tenure, they bridged the divide between street-oriented rap sensibilities and pop-focused vocal arrangements. Their 1990 track 'Let's Chill' further solidified their chart presence, peaking at number three on the US R&B charts, illustrating the enduring impact of Riley's swingbeat rhythmic patterns.",
